# No em dashes in user-facing copy

Do not use em dashes (`—`) anywhere in user-facing text (UI labels, headlines, body copy, errors, share text, metadata descriptions).

Prefer:
- periods
- commas
- parentheses
- colons

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<p>The postcard is the invitation — share it with friends.</p>

// ✅ GOOD
<p>The postcard is the invitation. Share it with friends.</p>
```

This does not apply to code operators, regex character classes, or non-user-facing comments unless those comments mirror product copy.
